# Wisp-Cursor bridge trigger

Follow `~/.cursor/skills/ws-continue/SKILL.md`
(project copy: `.cursor/skills/ws-continue/SKILL.md`).

After wiring, do the user's xxx (the rest of the sentence) if they already
specified work; otherwise do HANDOFF `next`. Check path + `mcp.json` once per
session. Do not re-run sync if the overlay is already present.

## Path (highest priority — no passphrase)

If the Cursor workspace root or `cwd` is under:

- `D:\AI4S_WispScience\`
- `D:/AI4S_WispScience/`
- case-insensitive `ai4s_wispscience`

then this **is** a Wisp Science (WS) topic folder. On the first relevant turn
(new chat, or user starts work), run `ws-continue` even with no spoken
passphrase.

Do **not** treat `D:\Cursor-task\WispScienceCursor化` as a science folder
even if someone mentions Wisp.

## Spoken phrases (still required when path is elsewhere)

Also fire if the user says any of these (or a close variant matching the
Pattern). These work even if the folder is **not** under the Wisp topics root
(example: `D:\AI4S_WispScience\`).

